Rebuild and confirm the digest is unchanged:

  bash tools/subset-font.sh
  sha256sum src/fonts/vazirmatn-arabic-subset.woff2

The Non-Latin build is deliberate: the system UI stack already renders Latin,
Cyrillic and CJK better than a subset would, and a Latin-bearing build costs
90 KB of base64 instead of 42 KB. The @font-face declaration carries the same
unicode-range, so the face is never applied to Latin text even when the
interface language is Persian or Arabic.
